The key distinction is that `m < n` need only be maintained when `n` is nonzero: if `n` is zero, the module cannot enter `DONE`. These two invariants are individually 1-inductive and together imply the target property. The overlapped implication `|->` checks each consequent in the same sampled cycle. ([accellera.org](https://www.accellera.org/images/resources/videos/SystemVerilog_Assertions_Tutorial_2016.pdf?utm_source=openai))

